  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 371fcced5420eda46b9cb39fda4431ce, type: 3}
  m_Name: Azalea
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FlowerData
  id: azalea
  displayName: Azalea
  scientificName: 'Rhododendron simsii '
  markerImageName: azalea
  description: Azalea is a compact evergreen shrub known for its abundant, funnel-shaped
    flowers in shades of pink, red, white, purple and orange. Rhododendron simsii
    is commonly grown as an indoor or greenhouse azalea. It has small, dark-green
    leaves and produces a colourful display during the cooler months. With suitable
    care, the plant can flower again in following seasons.
  origin: "East and Southeast Asia \u2014 southern China, Taiwan, parts of Indochina
    and the Ryukyu Islands of Japan"
  meaning: Femininity, gentleness, affection, gratitude and care. Azaleas can also
    represent temperance and the importance of looking after loved ones.
  habitat: Cool, humid forests, woodland margins, mountain slopes and rocky areas
    with acidic, well-drained soil.
  birthflower: Not an official traditional birth flower; commonly associated with
    spring
  floweringSeason: Naturally spring; indoor plants may flower from late autumn to
    spring when commercially forced
  sunlight: Bright, indirect light or partial shade. Protect it from intense midday
    and afternoon sunlight.
  watering: Keep the soil consistently moist but never waterlogged. Water when the
    surface begins to feel slightly dry. Rainwater or low-mineral water is preferable
    because azaleas dislike alkaline conditions.
  difficulty: Moderate
  flowerImage: {fileID: 0}
